Z||000000||David Bartlett||09-09-2001||09:01 PM||||I have a 86 2.8, and went to replace the bushings in the top motor mount, and found that the new urethane ones didn't fit. Did they make different dogbones for different years?||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||09-09-2001||09:21 PM||||yes<P>Now I can finish what I started.<P>v-6 had two dogbone styles. One with rib running outside of bone(poly will work), and one without(poly will not work, the d/b is oval, not round).<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 09-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||David Bartlett||09-10-2001||12:05 AM||||So when years came with the oval bones?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Captain Midnight||09-10-2001||02:31 AM||||I can machine your dogbone so your bushings will fit for $20.00.<P>------------------<BR>Captain Midnight||||reg||1
Z||000004||Nashco||09-10-2001||04:52 AM||||I bought a new dogbone housing from Darrell Morse for VERY cheap at a swap meet.  It was black powdercoated and made from TIG welded steel tubing.  It cost me the same price as Captain Midnight has offered to machine your old one for, except it looks GREAT.  Here's a pic of mine installed (apologize for the mess in there   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">)<P> <IMG SRC="http://home1.gte.net/jbnash/diamonddogbone.jpg">   <P>I can't remember his email or phone number, but if you do a search for Morse you will find it.<P>Oh, by the way, I got just the dogbone frame for that price; I ordered the poly bushings separately.  They're available from <A HREF="http://www.suspension.com" TARGET=_blank>www.suspension.com</A>  for the best price.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<P>[Strange..PIP didn't work]<p>[This message has been edited by Nashco (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||1
